e": "Hultgren", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 10053052, "full_name": "Herbert W. Virgin", "first_name": "Herbert W.", "last_name": "Virgin", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 376449, "full_name": "David A. Hunstad", "first_name": "David A.", "last_name": "Hunstad", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/Mannoside_treatment_attenuates_bladder_and_kidney_infection_/13666774", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p><b>A</b>) Schematic of mannoside treatment experiments. Male C3H/HeN mice were infected with UTI89; after 5 d, mice were administered mannoside 29R (8 mg/kg/dose intraperitoneally (IP)) or vehicle (mock treatment) every 8 h for either 24 or 48 h. <b>B</b>) Intratubular colonies of UPEC (teal) were observed 5 dpi in male C3H/HeN mice within desmoglein-2 positive (Dsg2+, red) collecting ducts (aquaporin-2 [AQP2]+, green). DAPI, blue; scale bar, 10 \u03bcm. Mannoside treatment for 24 h (<b>C</b>) significantly reduced bacterial loads in the bladder (*p = 0.0255) and kidneys (*p = 0.0434) (n = 8\u201310 mice per group over 2 independent experiments), while an even more significant effect was seen with 48 h treatment (<b>D</b>; bladder ***p = 0.0003, kidneys **p = 0.0042; n = 8 mice per group over 2 independent experiments).</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 1437304, "created_date": "2021-01-29T18:42:58Z", "modified_date": "2023-06-05T10:49:53Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["FimH mannose-binding pocket", "type 1 pilus-mediated pathogenesis", "FIM", "type 1 pilus adhesin", "kidney infection", "receptor", "uropathogenic Escherichia coli", "DSG", "type 1- piliated UPEC", "type 1 pili", "Escherichia coli pyelonephritis Typ...", "C 3H mice", "FimH-dependent UPEC binding", "CRISPR", "mannosylated extracellular domain"], "keywords": ["FimH mannose-binding pocket", "type 1 pilus-mediated pathogenesis", "FIM", "type 1 pilus adhesin", "kidney infection", "receptor", "uropathogenic Escherichia coli", "DSG", "type 1- piliated UPEC", "type 1 pili", "Escherichia coli pyelonephritis Typ...", "C 3H mice", "FimH-dependent UPEC binding", "CRISPR", "mannosylated extracellular domain"], "categories": [{"id": 1, "title": "Biophysics", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 4, "title": "Biochemistry", "parent_id": 38, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 7, "title": "Medicine", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 8, "title": "Microbiology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 12, "title": "Cell Biology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 13, "title": "Genetics", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 14, "title": "Molecular Biology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 19, "title": "Pharmacology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 46, "title": "Immunology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 734, "title": "Biological Sciences not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 62, "title": "Marine Biology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 64, "title": "Cancer", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 132, "title": "Infectious Diseases", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}], "references": ["https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.ppat.1009314"], "has_linked_file": false, "citation": "McL